Z||000005||cadero2dmax||12-29-2001||03:17 PM||||Depends a lot on what info you want, there isn't a lot of info that hasn't been covered here already.<P>If you compete in your Fiero (or just want to know how to make one handle better)there is another list availble specifically aimed at that interest group. You can also learn info about suspensions and detailed alignment specs that go one step beyond the info found here. Including how to setup your Fiero for a specific type of competition. If this is the case, then FieroRacingList@yahoogroups.com is an excellent source for that type info.<P>Then there are a ton of other Fiero lists out there, most are specific to one geographical area, or one type of modification (the Cadero owners forum for Cadillac powered Fieros, for example).<P>So, I guess you would need to know exactly what you are looking for in order to find another list or forum that will serve you nearly as well as PFF. Besides, this is the largest, therefore the most diversified list or forum of all Fiero related lists/forums out there. <P>Ain't much covered elsewhere that ain't already included here!!<P>------------------<BR>George Ryan<BR>A pair of 4.9 Cadero's<P>For Racing Photos of my former Q4 Fiero racecar, go to: <BR>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821 <P>(until I can figure out how to post photos)||||reg||1
